<article class="env-lemma" id="05XA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05XA">Lemma <span data-tag="05XA">76.49.3</span>.</a> Consider a commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X \ar[rr]_ f \ar[rd]_ p &  &  Y \ar[ld]^ q \\  &  Z }  \]
</div>
  <p> of algebraic spaces. Assume that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$p$ is locally of finite type, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$p$ is universally closed, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$q : Y \to Z$ is separated. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then there exists an open subspace $W \subset Z$ such that a morphism $Z' \to Z$ factors through $W$ if and only if the base change $f_{Z'} : X_{Z'} \to Y_{Z'}$ is a closed immersion. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We will use the characterization of closed immersions as universally closed, unramified, and universally injective morphisms, see Lemma <a href="/tag/05W8" data-tag="05W8">76.14.9</a>. First, note that since $p$ is universally closed and $q$ is separated, we see that $f$ is universally closed, see Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/04NX" data-tag="04NX">67.40.6</a>. It follows that any base change of $f$ is universally closed, see Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03IS" data-tag="03IS">67.9.3</a>. Thus to finish the proof of the lemma it suffices to prove that the assumptions of Lemma <a href="/tag/05X9" data-tag="05X9">76.49.2</a> are satisfied. The projection $\text{pr}_0 : X \times _ Y X \to X$ is universally closed as a base change of $f$, see Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03IS" data-tag="03IS">67.9.3</a>. Hence $X \times _ Y X \to Z$ is universally closed as a composition of universally closed morphisms (see Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03IU" data-tag="03IU">67.9.4</a>). This finishes the proof of the lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>